From d80ed332ba01aead6e739b38bc380d7c4eb61cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:51:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: harma: populate the FRU EEPROMs

Back six of the eight FRU EEPROMs with images read from hardware, so
guest firmware can identify the MB, MB NIC, PDB, SCM, BSM and Aegis
boards instead of finding them blank. The PTTV FRU was absent from the
sampled chassis and the retimer flash is not an IPMI FRU, so both stay
blank.

The content is sanitized: part and serial numbers masked, dates fixed,
asset tags replaced, distinct originals kept distinct. The MB NIC
carries an OEM MultiRecord whose contents are undocumented; the record
is kept and its body zeroed.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_harma.c | 256 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 250 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_harma.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_harma.c
index 326b348cd8..4df5855075 100644
--- a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_harma.c
+++ b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_harma.c
@@ -40,6 +40,244 @@
